<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16758" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσύμ-βᾰτος</span></b> , 
			Att.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀξ-,</span>
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>not coming to terms,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἀξ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					3.46
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἐχθρός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					1.223
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντι&lt;&gt;θεσις ἀ.</span>
			<i>irreconcilable,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.946e
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Procl.
				<u>Inst.</u>
				28
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dam.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				5
			</span></i>. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τως, ἔχειν</span> to be
				<i>irreconcilable,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				24
			</span></i> H., <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Cic.</u>
				46
			</span></i>: neut. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
			</span></i> as Adv., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσύμβατα μνησικακοῦντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					2.520
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>not comparable, disparate:</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς ἕτερα ἀ.</span>
			<i>incongruous</i> in other respects, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				5.540
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τραῦμα ἀ.</span> wound <i>that will not
				close up, heal,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Aret.
				<u>CA</u>
				2.2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Act.
			, <i>bringing no agreement,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοινολογία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					15.9.1
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
